----
fzf
----

The binary works on its own; the shell integration is not enabled
automatically and has to be sourced.

Bash completion is installed where bash finds it by itself, so the `**`
completion trigger works in a new shell with no further action.

The key bindings (CTRL-T, CTRL-R, ALT-C) and the zsh/fish integration must be
sourced explicitly. Add the line for your shell to its startup file:

  bash    source <prefix>/share/fzf/shell/key-bindings.bash

  zsh     source <prefix>/share/fzf/shell/completion.zsh
          source <prefix>/share/fzf/shell/key-bindings.zsh

  fish    source <prefix>/share/fzf/shell/completion.fish
          source <prefix>/share/fzf/shell/key-bindings.fish

`fzf-tmux` is installed in <prefix>/bin and needs terminal/tmux.

An example preview helper is available at
<prefix>/share/fzf/fzf-preview.sh, for use with --preview.

Integration files for nushell are not shipped, as nushell is not packaged
for OmniOS.
